      "descriptions": [
        {
          "value": "George VI became king in December 1936 following the abdication of Edward VIII. Neville Chamberlain became prime minister in May 1937 and was a Conservative politician. The monarchy and premiership are shown as distinct offices, with separate periods of service. Chamberlain’s foreign policy sought to avoid another European war through negotiation and concessions; the Munich agreement of 1938 was a central expression of that policy. These leadership records apply to the requested year, rather than the nearest boundary snapshot. Relationships shown elsewhere from the map’s SUBJECTO and PARTOF fields retain their original dataset meaning and are not a substitute for a constitutional account of Britain’s imperial possessions.",
